# Semantic CAD/BIM client walkthrough — GENERATED by ggen (templates/walkthrough.md.tera)

Design-decode events flow: browser console -> `smaltFetch` -> emulator planes.
Networking seam: `workspace/lib/smalt.ts` (`smaltFetch`, loopback-only; raw
`fetch` is ESLint-banned). Control plane 9443, data plane 8443.

## 1. Design decode (binary artifact -> events)

Point the console at a design artifact already in Blob (WORM — immutable model
revisions: `blob_storage.ex:273`, immutabilityPolicy routes
`egress_router.ex:1313`). The decode activity emits one event per element with
its storey containment and geometry payload:

| element | storey | geometry | format |
|---|---|---|---|
{% for row in elements -%}
| `{{ row.element }}` | `{{ row.storey }}` | `{{ row.geometry }}` | {{ row.format }} |
{% endfor %}

## 2. Blob artifact store (write-once)

POST the decoded artifact to the Blob container (data plane 8443). The
artifact is content-addressed (`cad:artifactDigest`, e.g. `sha256:...`):
identical bytes, identical digest — Blob WORM makes revision churn without
byte change unrepresentable.

## 3. Cosmos temporal KG documents

For each revision, PUT one KG document per valid-time interval
(`CosmosRoutes.ex:61-205`, ETag CAS `cosmos.ex:133` for bitemporal
versioning — optimistic concurrency on the document `_etag`).

## 4. Temporal query walkthrough (revision chain = time travel)

The revision chain is the time-travel axis. Each non-root revision carries
`prov:wasRevisionOf` to its predecessor; the root (`cad:RootRevision`,
index 0) is the chain anchor.

| revision | index | predecessor |
|---|---|---|
{% for row in chain -%}
| `{{ row.revision }}` | {{ row.index }} | {{ row.predecessor }} |
{% endfor %}

To travel to revision N: query Cosmos for documents whose `validFrom <= N`'s
generatedAtTime and (`validUntil` absent OR `validUntil` > that instant).
The KG view at revision N is exactly the design as of that revision — no
recomputation, only valid-time selection.

## 5. Refusal surface (what the gates refuse)

1. **Element without storey containment** — a `bot:Element` with no
   missing `bot:hasElement` membership from a `bot:Storey` refuses (gates/010).
2. **Revision without predecessor** — a `cad:DesignRevision` with no
   `prov:wasRevisionOf`, unless it is `cad:RootRevision`, refuses (gates/020).
3. **Orphan geometry** — a `cad:Geometry` claimed by no element refuses
   (gates/030).

Authority: this walkthrough is a projection; generated artifacts claim NONE
and stand UNKNOWN until a consumer court admits them.
